.TH RUNTIMES 1 "2026-08-29" "dots" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runtimes \- manage project runtimes declared in .runtimesrc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runtimes
.RI < command " [" args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B runtimes
is the CLI half of the direnv integration: it reads a project's
.IR .runtimesrc ,
resolves each declared runtime through its backend, and records the
concrete result in the project's
.IR .runtimes.lock .
It is deployed as
.I ~/bin/runtimes
by
.BR dots\-setup (1)
from
.IR common/bin/bin/runtimes ;
the direnv half is documented in
.IR docs/direnv\-runtimes.md .
.PP
Three backends, one resolution rule each:
.TP
.B python \(-> uv
Any uv-resolvable spec
.RI ( 3.12 ,
.RI 3.12.7 ),
installed via
.BR "uv python install" .
.TP
.B node \(-> fnm
A major
.RI ( 22 )
resolves to the latest
.B vX.Y.Z
via
.B fnm ls\-remote
at install time; a concrete
.B vX.Y.Z
(or
.BR X.Y.Z )
is used verbatim.
.TP
.B java \(-> sdkman
A major
.RI ( 17 )
resolves to the latest
.B <major>.x.y\-amzn
(Corretto) via the sdkman version API, falling back to
.B <major>.x.y\-tem
(Temurin) when a major has no Corretto build \(em
.B sdk list
is never used because it forces a pager; an exact candidate ID
.RI ( 21.0.12+1.1\-amzn )
is used verbatim.
.PP
.B ensure
is the direnv hot path: it only reads local files, so a satisfied project is
a milliseconds-fast no-op. Anything missing or changed kicks off a detached
install
.RB ( "nohup \(ha " " &" )
whose output goes to a per-project log, so
.I .envrc
evaluation never blocks on the network. A pid guard under
.I ~/.local/state/runtimes/pids
makes installs single-flight: while one runs, further
.B ensure
calls print one status line and exit 0. When the install finishes it writes
.I .runtimes.lock
atomically (temp file + rename), so a project never sees a half-applied
environment.
.PP
stdout is reserved for
.B path
output (machine-consumed by the direnv helpers); every human-facing message
goes to stderr.
.SS "The lock file"
.I .runtimes.lock
holds one line per runtime, recording the resolved version and the absolute
store path:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python 3.12 3.12.12 ~/.local/share/uv/python/cpython\-3.12.12\-macos\-x86_64\-none
node 22 22.21.1 ~/.local/share/fnm/node\-versions/v22.21.1/installation
java 17 17.0.20\-amzn ~/.sdkman/candidates/java/17.0.20\-amzn
.fi
.RE
.PP
The lock is written only when every entry in
.I .runtimesrc
is satisfied \(em a failed line leaves the old lock in place (and the
detached worker reports
.BR "install incomplete \(ha \(em lock not written" )
so the next
.B cd
retries the whole install.
.I .envrc
evaluation reads the lock, never the network and never resolution logic.
.SS Commands
.TP
.BI "ensure " [ dir ]
Satisfy every runtime in
.IR <dir>/.runtimesrc
(default: the current directory, also the fallback for a relative
.IR dir ).
Exits 0 immediately when there is no
.IR .runtimesrc ,
when the lock already covers every entry with a live store path, when an
install is in flight
.RB ( "install still in progress (\(ha); log: \(ha" ),
or after kicking off a new detached install
.RB ( "installing python 3.12, node 22 (log: \(ha)" ).
On BSD, prints
.BR "runtime auto\-install unsupported on BSD; falling back to system runtimes" ,
checks
.BR "command \-v"
per name, and exits 0.
.TP
.BI "install " "<name> <version>"
Foreground install of one runtime with visible progress; the same
resolution and atomicity rules as
.BR ensure ,
but it fails (exit 1) instead of degrading. Refused outright on BSD.
.TP
.B status
List installed runtimes per backend
.RB ( "uv python list \-\-only\-installed" ,
fnm
.IR node\-versions/ ,
sdkman candidates except
.BR current )
plus the store and state paths, and the project
.I .runtimesrc
and
.I .runtimes.lock
when the current directory has one.
.TP
.BI "path " "<name> <spec> [ dir ]"
Print the runtime's bin dir (python, node) or
.B JAVA_HOME
(java) from
.IR <dir>/.runtimes.lock
(default: the current directory); this is what the direnv helpers consume.
Exit 1 when the lock has no matching entry
.RB ( "<name> <spec> not satisfied in <dir>" )
or when the entry points at a path that no longer exists.
.TP
.BI "template " "<name> [\-\-force] [ dest ]"
Expand the repo template
.I templates/<name>
into
.I dest
(default: the current directory).
.B {{VAR}}
tokens in file contents are substituted from the environment variables listed
in the manifest's
.B substitute=
line (unset vars are left in place with a warning). Existing files are never
overwritten unless
.B \-\-force
.RB ( "refusing to overwrite:\(ha" ).
Manifest files matched by
.B ignore=
globs are skipped. Everything is staged first and moved per file, so the
destination only ever gains whole files.
.SS "Platform support"
.TP
.B Full
macOS (x86_64, aarch64), Debian/Ubuntu, Alpine x86_64, WSL2
(Debian/Alpine x86_64): direnv, uv, fnm and sdkman are installed by
.BR dots\-setup (1);
all three backends auto-install.
.TP
.B Partial
Alpine/WSL aarch64 (musl): python and java auto-install as usual; node has no
arm64-musl build \(em the install dies with
.BR "no musl node build for <arch>: unofficial\-builds ships x64\-musl only" .
Alpine x86_64 node comes from the unofficial-builds mirror via
.B FNM_NODE_DIST_MIRROR
and
.BR "FNM_ARCH=x64\-musl" .
.TP
.B "Dotfiles only"
FreeBSD and other
.B *BSD
names: configs (including the direnv package) deploy, but runtime
auto-install is unsupported:
.B ensure
degrades to system runtimes via
.B "command \-v"
and exits 0;
.B install
refuses with an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage to stderr and exit 0 (bare
.B runtimes
does the same).
.TP
.B \-\-force
With
.B template
only: overwrite existing files at the destination.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Base for every default store, the state dir and
.IR ~/bin/runtimes .
.TP
.B FNM_DIR
fnm store; defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share/fnm .
Node installs land in
.IR $FNM_DIR/node\-versions/vX.Y.Z/installation .
.TP
.B UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR
uv's python store; defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share/uv/python .
Honored by uv itself during installs; shown by
.BR status .
.TP
.B SDKMAN_DIR
sdkman root; defaults to
.IR ~/.sdkman .
Java candidates live in
.IR $SDKMAN_DIR/candidates/java/<id> .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or a path designed not to fail evaluation:
.B ensure
kicked off (or found running) a detached install;
.B ensure
on BSD fell back to system runtimes;
.B \-\-help
was printed.
.TP
.B 1
An error: unknown command, wrong argument count, no such directory, unknown
runtime name (supported: python, node, java), a backend failure
.RB ( uv ,
.BR fnm ,
or sdkman missing; no release matching the spec),
.B path
on an unsatisfied runtime, or a template refusing to overwrite. A detached
worker whose install was incomplete also exits 1 \(em after writing no lock.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .runtimesrc
Per-project runtime declarations, one
.RI < name " " < spec >
per line;
.B #
starts a comment.
.TP
.I .runtimes.lock
Per-project resolved versions and store paths, written by
.BR ensure 's
detached worker.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/runtimes/logs/<hash>.log
Output of the detached install for a project.
.I <hash>
is a hash of the project directory path
.RB ( sha256sum ,
.RB "shasum \-a 256" ,
or
.BR cksum ,
whichever exists).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/runtimes/pids/<hash>.pid
Single-flight guard for the detached install; a marker whose pid is dead is
reclaimed.
.TP
.IR ~/.local/share/uv/python ", " $FNM_DIR/node\-versions ", " $SDKMAN_DIR/candidates/java
The per-backend stores.
.TP
.IR templates/<name>/ ", " templates/<name>.template
In the repo (not stowed): the template tree and its manifest
.RB ( description= ,
.RB substitute= ,
.BR ignore= ).
Located relative to the repo root, derived from the script's own location so
the stowed symlink resolves into the clone.
.SH EXAMPLES
Declare a project's runtimes and let direnv drive the CLI:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&$ cd ~/code/foo
\&$ printf 'python 3.12\ennode 22\en' > .runtimesrc
\&$ runtimes ensure
==> runtimes: installing python 3.12, node 22 (log: \(ha)
\&$ runtimes ensure
==> runtimes: install still in progress (python 3.12, node 22); log: \(ha
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect the stores and the current project through
.BR just (1):
.PP
.RS
.nf
just runtimes status
.fi
.RE
.PP
Consume a locked runtime the way the direnv helpers do (stdout only):
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&$ runtimes path python 3.12
/Users/you/.local/share/uv/python/cpython\-3.12.12\-macos\-aarch64\-none/bin
\&$ runtimes path java 17
/Users/you/.sdkman/candidates/java/17.0.20\-amzn
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR docs/direnv\-runtimes.md ,
.BR dots\-setup (1),
.BR loadavg (1),
.BR tmux\-copy (1)